11.0.0 — what a value does, zoom at the side, several notes at once, nothing hidden

New since 10084, built by the Echoel Studio run; nothing here is device-verified yet.
- Modulation: each route's row shows its source's reading as a bar and what it adds now ("+12.5 %"),
  or "Not measured"; it moves, it never blinks.
- Zoom: a strip at the right edge of Arrange and of the note editor — touch or drag to zoom,
  double-tap for the standard size, VoiceOver adjusts it a step at a time. Buttons and pinch stay.
- Note editor: Select More chooses several notes; Delete, Quantize, Humanize, Strum and Revoice act
  on all of them, and dragging one moves them all, keeping their shape at the clip's edges.
- Doors that were only behind a hold: a tap on an audio region opens its settings; Add Marker in
  Arrange's zoom bar; Automate, Modulate and Effects in the track list's menu; Automate and
  Modulate on the Mixer's master strip; Follow Pulse (Flow) in Song › Play and Sync; the
  arpeggiator at the top of the Sound page.
- Arrange: a button in the zoom bar shows or hides the modulation rows; hidden routes still play.
- Learn: a chapter "The Instrument and the Body" (Body Voice, Mood, Flow).
- Fixed: an effect page kept "Loading…" under its values and a grey Compare after the effect had
  loaded.
Limits, new: several notes are chosen with the Select More switch, not by drawing a frame; the
note editor zooms in four sizes; the drum step grid has no zoom strip yet.
Still: a sample click above 300 BPM is cut by the next one. Older limits as in 10083.

Previous: 10084. A green commit that changes this file uploads build 10000 + run number. A test
list, not a source for claims (ContentPipeline/CLAIMS.md).

One ask, as for 10083 and 10084. Start a screen recording, open the app, and try to make sixteen
bars in two to five minutes: a beat, a bass line or a chord, then Play. No list and no protocol; stop wherever
it stops being possible or pleasant. The recording is the answer. What gets in the way in it is
the next work, in the order it happened.

The five checks of 10079 stay open and unchanged and rest until that recording exists.
